  "finish": {
    "summary": "Five drawers in one base isn't possible here. Drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base. A half base has one cut face, so it holds one drawer. A full base and a quarter base each offered no drawer slots. I swapped the full base for a north half base and added the one drawer it takes. The build passes all checks and the meshes clear. The only other note is that three open faces could take caps.",
    "requirements": [
      {
        "requirement": "A single hex base",
        "status": "met",
        "evidence": "The only base is piece:0,0,0;half-n. I swapped the original full base for this half because the full base offered no drawer slots."
      },
      {
        "requirement": "Nothing else added beside or on top of it",
        "status": "met",
        "evidence": "Nothing else is on the build: no neighbouring cells, nothing on top. The only added part is the drawer inside the base."
      },
      {
        "requirement": "Five drawers in it",
        "status": "unmet",
        "evidence": "Only 1 drawer fits (drawer:0#0,0#cut). After I placed it, no more drawer slots were offered. Full and quarter bases offered none at all."
      }
    ]
